        "title": "National Scholarships & Taxability of Grants (Section 10(16))",
        "content": "Scholarships free financial assistance hoti hai — ise kabhie wapas nahi lautana padta! India mein har saal **hazaaron crore rupees** ki government scholarships un-claimed reh jaati hain kyunki students ko eligibility portal workflows aur document verification rules ka pata nahi hota.\n\n---\n\n### 19.2.1 National Scholarship Portal (NSP) — Master Guide & Verification Workflow\n\n**National Scholarship Portal (`scholarship.gov.in`)** Government of India ka centralized digital platform hai jahan Central Ministries, State Governments, aur UT Administrations ki 50+ major scholarship schemes operates hoti hain.\n\n```\n                  [Step 1: Student OTR (One Time Registration) via Aadhaar]\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n                  [Step 2: Scheme Selection & Application Submission]\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n               [Level-1 (L1): Institute Verification Officer (INO) Verification]\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n               [Level-2 (L2): District Nodal Officer (DNO) Verification]\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n               [Level-3 (L3): State Nodal Officer (SNO) / Ministry Approval]\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n               [PFMS (Public Financial Management System) Verification]\n                                              │\n                                              ▼\n               [Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) via Aadhaar Payment Bridge System (APBS)]\n```\n\n#### Major Central Government Scholarship Schemes on NSP (Table 19.5)\n\n| Category / Scheme Name | Eligibility Criteria & Income Cap | Annual Financial Support | Nodal Ministry / Department |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **PM-USP Central Sector Scheme for College/University Students** | Top 20th percentile in Class 12 Board Exams. Family Income < **₹4.50 LPA**. Age 18-25. | **₹12,000/yr** for 1st 3 yrs (Graduation)<br>**₹20,000/yr** for Post-Graduation. | Department of Higher Education, Ministry of Education (MoE) |\n| **Post-Matric Scholarship for SC/ST Students** | SC/ST students studying in Class 11 up to Ph.D. Family Income < **₹2.50 LPA**. | **100% Non-refundable tuition fee waiver** + Up to **₹13,500/year** hostel/maintenance allowance. | Ministry of Social Justice / Ministry of Tribal Affairs |\n| **Merit-cum-Means (MCM) Scholarship for Minorities** | Minority Communities (Muslim, Christian, Sikh, Jain, Buddhist, Parsi). >50% marks in 12th. Income < **₹2.50 LPA**. | **₹20,000/year** course fee reimbursement + **₹1,000/month** maintenance allowance (10 months/yr). | Ministry of Minority Affairs |\n| **PM YASASVI Post-Matric Scholarship** | OBC, EBC (Economically Backward), and DNT Students. Family Income < **₹2.50 LPA**. | **₹4,000 to ₹20,000/year** based on level of study. | Ministry of Social Justice & Empowerment |\n| **Top Class Education Scheme for SC/ST Students** | Admission in notified premier institutes (IITs, NITs, IIMs, AIIMS, NIFTs, NLUs). Family Income < **₹8.00 LPA**. | **100% Full Tuition Fee** + ₹86,000 first year computer allowance + ₹3,000/month living cost + ₹5,000/yr books. | Ministry of Social Justice & Empowerment |\n\n#### Critical NSP Rules — Preventing Application Rejection:\n1. **Aadhaar Payment Bridge System (APBS):** NSP transfers cash ONLY via Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) using Aadhaar-seeded bank accounts.\n2. **Bank Account Seeding vs Linking:** Aadhaar *linking* (giving Aadhaar copy to bank) is NOT enough! Your bank account must be **NPCI Mapper Seeded** for DBT processing. Visit your bank branch and request: *\"Please map my account in NPCI Mapper for DBT Aadhaar payments.\"*\n3. **Strict One Scholarship Rule:** Government financial rules state that a student can draw **ONLY ONE government scholarship** in a single financial year. If you apply for both State Post-Matric and Central NSP scheme, automated PFMS deduplication algorithms will flag your Aadhaar and cancel BOTH applications!\n\n#### How to Check NPCI Aadhaar Seeding Status:\n- **Method A (Bank App):** Log into SBI YONO, PNB One, or your bank's mobile app -> Go to *Services -> Aadhaar Seeding / DBT Status*.\n- **Method B (Bank Branch):** Submit a written request: *\"Application for Seeding Aadhaar in NPCI Mapping for receiving Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) Payouts.\"* Obtain a stamped acknowledgment.\n- **Method C (UIDAI Portal):** Visit `myaadhaar.uidai.gov.in` -> Click *Bank Seeding Status* (Requires Aadhaar OTP).\n\n---\n\n### 19.2.2 AICTE Special Scholarship Schemes — Pragati, Saksham & Swanath\n\nTechnical education (Engineering, Architecture, Pharmacy, Hotel Management, Management) pursue karne wale students ke liye **AICTE (All India Council for Technical Education)** teen mega scholarship programs chalata hai:\n\n#### 1. AICTE Pragati Scholarship Scheme for Female Students\n- **Target Audience:** Girl students admitted to 1st year (or 2nd year via Lateral Entry) of AICTE-approved Technical Diploma/Degree institutions.\n- **Total Quota:** **10,000 Scholarships Annually** (5,000 for Degree + 5,000 for Diploma). In addition, ALL eligible girl students from 13 North Eastern states and Union Territories (J&K, Ladakh, etc.) are given scholarships without quota limits!\n- **Eligibility:** Gross annual family income must be **< ₹8.00 Lakhs Per Annum**. Maximum 2 girl children per family.\n- **Financial Grant:** **₹50,000 Per Annum** for every year of study (4 years for B.Tech = ₹2,00,000 Total!).\n- **Usage Flexibility:** Paid as a lump sum DBT transfer. Can be used for college fee payment, computer/laptop purchase, books, stationaries, equipment, and hostel charges.\n\n#### 2. AICTE Saksham Scholarship Scheme for Differently-Abled Students\n- **Target Audience:** Specially-abled students having a certified disability of **not less than 40%**.\n- **Eligibility:** Admitted to AICTE approved technical courses. Family income **< ₹8.00 LPA**.\n- **Financial Grant:** **₹50,000 Per Annum** for course duration. All eligible disabled students who apply receive the grant (No upper quota cap!).\n\n#### 3. AICTE Swanath Scholarship Scheme\n- **Target Categories:** \n  1. Orphan students.\n  2. Children whose parents died due to COVID-19.\n  3. Children of Armed Forces and Paramilitary Personnel martyred in action (Shaheed).\n- **Financial Support:** **₹50,000 Per Annum** for course duration + mentoring support.",
