        "title": "National Scholarships & Taxability of Grants (Section 10(16)) (Part 2)",
        "content": "#### AICTE Fellowship Schemes Breakdown (Table 19.6)\n\n| Scheme Name | Beneficiary | Grant Amount | Key Condition |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **AICTE Pragati** | Girl Students in Tech Courses | **₹50,000 / year** | Family Income < ₹8 LPA. Max 2 girls/family. |\n| **AICTE Saksham** | Differently-Abled Students (≥40%) | **₹50,000 / year** | Family Income < ₹8 LPA. All eligible covered. |\n| **AICTE Swanath** | Orphans / COVID victims / Shaheed children | **₹50,000 / year** | Verified certificate from District Collector / Defense Dept. |\n| **AICTE PG Scholarship** | GATE / GPAT Qualified M.Tech / M.Pharm students | **₹12,400 / month** (₹1,48,800/yr) | Valid GATE/GPAT score card + 24 months duration. |\n| **AICTE Doctoral Fellowship (ADF)** | Full-time Ph.D. scholars in AICTE thrust areas | **₹37,000/mo** (Yr 1-2) + **₹42,000/mo** (Yr 3) + HRA | Valid GATE/NET score + Age < 30 years. |\n\n---\n\n### 19.2.3 Section 10(16) Income Tax Exemption — Tax Rules for Scholarships & Stipends\n\nYeh topic students, researchers, aur unke parents ke liye sabse bada confusion rehta hai: \n*\"Kya student scholarship ya college research stipend par Income Tax dena padta hai?\"* \n*\"Kya Form 26AS / AIS mein stipend credit hone par ITR file karna padega?\"*\n\nLet me give you a detailed breakdown of **Section 10(16) of the Income Tax Act, 1961**!\n\n#### The Statutory Provision of Section 10(16):\n> *\"Scholarships granted to meet the cost of education are EXEMPT from Income Tax.\"*\n\n#### Key Legal Principles & Landmark Income Tax Appellate Tribunal (ITAT) Rulings:\n\n1. **Meaning of \"Cost of Education\":** The word \"education\" is not restricted to school/college tuition fees. It includes living expenses, hostel fees, purchase of books, research apparatus, travel for conferences, and day-to-day maintenance during studies.\n2. **No Employer-Employee Relationship:** If the money is granted to support learning, study, or independent scientific research, it is classified as a Scholarship/Fellowship and is **100% TAX-FREE**.\n3. **Service Rendered Test:** If the institution pays you money specifically in return for operational services rendered (e.g., teaching undergraduate classes, checking 500 exam papers, working as an office clerk), that specific portion is treated as Salary Income and is TAXABLE.\n\n#### Taxability Matrix for Various Student Inflow Types (Table 19.7)\n\n| Student Income Type | Taxability Status | Relevant Section | Tax Treatment & ITR Reporting |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Merit / Need Scholarships** (NSP, Pragati, Foundation Grants) | **100% TAX-EXEMPT** | Section 10(16) | Show under *Exempt Income* schedule in ITR-1. Tax Payable = ₹0. |\n| **Research Fellowships (JRF / SRF / CSIR / DST / UGC)** | **100% TAX-EXEMPT** | Section 10(16) | Tax-Free. ITAT Kolkata in *Dr. V. Mahadev vs CIT* confirmed research fellowships are exempt. |\n| **PMRF (Prime Minister's Research Fellowship)** | **100% TAX-EXEMPT** | Section 10(16) | Even though amount is ₹70,000 - ₹80,000/month, full amount is exempt as cost of education! |\n| **Teaching Assistantship (TA) / Assistant Honorarium** | **TAXABLE** | Section 192 / Head: Salary | Taxable under Salary / Other Sources if paid for specific teaching duties assigned by university. |\n| **Corporate Internship Stipend** (Private Company Work) | **TAXABLE** | Head: Salary / Other Sources | Taxable above basic exemption limit. Company may deduct TDS u/s 194J or 192. |\n| **PM Internship Scheme Stipend** (Govt Corporate Scheme) | **TAX-EXEMPT** | Special CBDT Circular / Sec 10 | Stipend up to ₹5,000/month + ₹6,000 grant falls below basic exemption limit (₹3L/4L). |\n\n#### How to Report Section 10(16) Exempt Income on e-Filing ITR Portal:\n1. Log into `incometax.gov.in` -> Click *e-File -> Income Tax Returns -> File Income Tax Return*.\n2. Select **ITR-1 (Sahaj)** or **ITR-2** based on your overall income sources.\n3. Under **Gross Total Income**, navigate to **Exempt Income** schedule.\n4. Click *Add Exempt Income* -> Select dropdown code **Section 10(16) - Scholarships granted to meet the cost of education**.\n5. Enter the exact annual fellowship/scholarship amount received.\n6. This ensures your bank credit matches your tax return while officially declaring **₹0 Taxable Income** on that amount!\n\n---\n\n### 19.2.4 High-Value National Research Fellowships — DST-INSPIRE & PMRF Tax Treatment\n\nScience, Technology, Engineering, aur Mathematics (STEM) graduates ke liye India mein world-class research fellowships exist karti hain.",
